  1. Create the akwaaba-indexer service account, with no login shell
     $ useradd --system --home /srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer --shell /usr/sbin/nologin akwaaba-indexer
  2. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/projects exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/projects
  3. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/deployments exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/deployments
  4. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/configs exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/configs
  5. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/logs exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/logs
  6. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/systemd exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/systemd
  7. Ensure /srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer exists, owned by akwaaba-indexer
     $ install -d -o akwaaba-indexer -g akwaaba-indexer -m 750 /srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer
  8. Ensure /srv/solanaghana/deployments/akwaaba-indexer exists, owned by akwaaba-indexer
     $ install -d -o akwaaba-indexer -g akwaaba-indexer -m 750 /srv/solanaghana/deployments/akwaaba-indexer
  9. Ensure /srv/solanaghana/logs/akwaaba-indexer exists, owned by akwaaba-indexer
     $ install -d -o akwaaba-indexer -g akwaaba-indexer -m 750 /srv/solanaghana/logs/akwaaba-indexer
 10. Fetch the backend repository at production
     $ git clone --depth 1 --branch production https://github.com/user/akwaaba-indexer /srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer/backend
 11. Build the backend
     $ cd /srv/solanaghana/projects/akwaaba-indexer/backend && cargo build --release
 12. Install the backend systemd unit
     $ install -o root -g root -m 644 /srv/solanaghana/systemd/akwaaba-indexer-backend.service /etc/systemd/system/akwaaba-indexer-backend.service
 13. Reload systemd so the new units are visible
     $ systemctl daemon-reload
 14. Enable and start the backend
     $ systemctl enable --now akwaaba-indexer-backend.service
 15. No domain is configured, so Caddy is left untouched
